WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.814
One amino acid swap,

2
00:00:01.834 --> 00:00:05.495
cysteine to arginine at position 112,

3
00:00:05.515 --> 00:00:08.513
is a major genetic risk factor for late-onset

4
00:00:08.533 --> 00:00:13.993
Alzheimer's disease. Yet in automated APOE4 literature mining,

5
00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:17.887
extraction struggled where science depends on it most:

6
00:00:17.926 --> 00:00:22.635
grounding every claim in primary experimental data.

7
00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:24.458
For the MecCog Challenge,

8
00:00:24.478 --> 00:00:28.231
Team Khepri paired a strict Step 1 extraction pipeline

9
00:00:28.251 --> 00:00:32.288
with an interactive Mol* 3D workbench.

10
00:00:32.327 --> 00:00:36.463
Under Rule C5, our Excel spreadsheets hold only

11
00:00:36.483 --> 00:00:39.365
verbatim literature quotes, panel locations,

12
00:00:39.385 --> 00:00:44.125
and printed statistics, separated cleanly from 3D structural

13
00:00:44.145 --> 00:00:45.859
models.

14
00:00:45.867 --> 00:00:49.388
In crystal structure 1B68,

15
00:00:49.408 --> 00:00:56.784
APOE4's Arg112 forms a 2.53 Å salt bridge with

16
00:00:56.804 --> 00:01:06.211
Glu109, displacing Arg61 outward from 3.53 to 5.34 Å

17
00:01:06.231 --> 00:01:10.599
compared to APOE3 structure 1NFN,

18
00:01:10.619 --> 00:01:14.447
consistent with altered domain interaction.

19
00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:18.325
Across two hypotheses, that structural shift is hypothesized

20
00:01:18.345 --> 00:01:20.914
to drive two organellar choke points.

21
00:01:20.934 --> 00:01:26.161
Under H2, impaired NHE6 proton-leak regulation traps ApoER2

22
00:01:26.181 --> 00:01:29.846
and LRP1 receptors in early endosomes.

23
00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:35.566
Under H5, ABCA1 and NPC1 lipid-export defects sequester

24
00:01:35.586 --> 00:01:40.616
cholesterol in lysosomes, elevating lysosomal pH and blunting

25
00:01:40.636 --> 00:01:43.093
beta-amyloid clearance.

26
00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:47.109
Every line is reproducible and physician-audited:

27
00:01:47.129 --> 00:01:52.298
30 entries covering 28 unique primary papers across H5

28
00:01:52.318 --> 00:01:57.198
and H2, yielding 120 experimental findings,

29
00:01:57.218 --> 00:02:02.427
126 printed-in-text statistics with panel locations,

30
00:02:02.466 --> 00:02:05.453
0 retracted or review papers,

31
00:02:05.473 --> 00:02:10.612
and 0 errors or warnings under strict validation.

32
00:02:10.633 --> 00:02:14.050
Honest boundaries matter just as much as support:

33
00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:17.707
we report 29 contradicting findings directly in the

34
00:02:17.727 --> 00:02:23.105
sheets. Neuronal NHE6 ablation rescues ApoER2 trafficking in

35
00:02:23.125 --> 00:02:28.457
vivo, whereas APOE4 astrocytes lose NHE6 and require

36
00:02:28.477 --> 00:02:33.914
NHE6 activation; H2 rests purely on Tier 2 models,

37
00:02:33.934 --> 00:02:38.628
and 4 gated or paywalled papers remain abstract-only rather

38
00:02:38.648 --> 00:02:40.884
than bypassed.

39
00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:44.595
28 unique papers across 30 entries.

40
00:02:44.615 --> 00:02:50.370
120 verified findings. 29 contradicting lines.

41
00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:54.104
Open the live 3D workbench and inspect every

42
00:02:54.124 --> 00:02:56.244
workbook on GitHub.
